│ patch_description        │ Replace the alternating-probe gradient estimate with a smoothed stagnation signal.        │
│                          │ Generation-to-generation fitness changes also reflect selection and population noise, so  │
│                          │ attributing them to probe direction can mislead width adaptation. Instead, pull mutation  │
│                          │ width toward a bounded target that increases when quality is low and progress stalls,     │
│                          │ while reducing exploration when the archive outperforms the population. Preserve          │
│                          │ decline-triggered recovery and reduce probe amplitude to limit disruption. This rule uses │
│                          │ only observed feedback and persistent memory; its effect on combined_score requires       │
│                          │ evaluation.                                                                               │
